      "obligation": "refuter:6:2",
      "id": "thm-valuative-criterion-separatedness",
      "location": "Statement, final sentence",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The sentence says the criterion “includes in particular all finite-type morphisms.” The dependency def-locally-finite-type-and-finite-type-morphism defines finite type as quasi-compact and locally of finite type; this does not imply quasi-separatedness over arbitrary bases. For example, let S = Spec k[x_1,x_2,...] and W = union_i D(x_i), which is not quasi-compact. Gluing two copies of S along W gives a quasi-compact, locally finite type morphism X → S, hence a finite-type morphism, whose diagonal is not quasi-compact: over the open S obtained as the product of the two charts, its inverse image is W. Thus the theorem's quasi-separatedness hypothesis excludes finite-type morphisms, contrary to this sentence.",
